# US Company Financial Statements from SEC XBRL (annual, last 12 months)

Standardised annual income statement, balance sheet and cash-flow lines for 5,494 US-listed companies, fiscal years ending in the last 12 months (5,537 company-years): revenue, gross profit, operating income, net income, EPS, cash, assets, liabilities, equity, operating cash flow, capex, dividends and buybacks.

```python
import pandas as pd
df = pd.read_parquet("hf://datasets/FinzData/sec-financial-statements/data/annual_statements.parquet")
df[df.ticker == "AAPL"]
```

**In the full FinzData dataset:** quarterly, annual and trailing-twelve-month statements since 2009, point-in-time (as filed on any past date) for backtests without look-ahead bias (`yf.Ticker("AAPL").quarterly_income_stmt`).

## Get the full history
This is a free sample. FinzData serves the complete dataset through its API and Python client
(`pip install finzdata`), with daily updates, alongside survivorship-free US stock prices since 2000,
COT positioning, 13F holdings, point-in-time fundamentals and macro data.

- Free API key: https://api.finzdata.com/
- Pricing (history bundles from $195 once): https://finzdata.com/pricing
- Guides: https://finzdata.com/guides
- Python client (open source): https://github.com/FinzData-com/finzdata-python

Data for research, not investment advice. Compiled by FinzData from public U.S. government sources.


